enus: own codepoints for Western extended characters

US English declares its extended Western characters (enye, acute
vowels, diaeresis, cedilla) so UTF-8 callers convert to the same bytes
Western callers hand over, instead of arriving as mojibake. Identity
mappings; behaviour for Western input is unchanged (the converter
leaves non-UTF-8 alone). Generated table via codepoints.py.
Applied at build time so CI builds the same tree.
